2026-11-19 21:06:06 - Agent_20261119210411 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed all 6 queries against requests 2.30.0 source. Confirmed the package is version 2.30.0 (requests/__version__.py:8), i.e. pre-fix for CVE-2023-32681 (proxy credential leak on cross-host redirect) and CVE-2024-35195 (TLS verify state leaking via connection-pool reuse).

True positives submitted (4):
1. requests/sessions.py:315-328 — rebuild_proxies() unconditionally re-attaches Proxy-Authorization via `_basic_auth_str(username, password)` without the `not scheme.startswith("https")` guard added in 2.31.0; combined with rebuild_auth() only stripping "Authorization" (line 291) and resolve_redirects calling rebuild_proxies() before rebuild_auth() (lines 244-245), proxy credentials follow cross-host redirects.
2. requests/sessions.py:317 additionally saved the deletion/re-add logic context.
3. requests/adapters.py:331 — cert_verify() mutates conn.cert_reqs/conn.ca_certs on an already-pooled connection; get_connection() takes no `verify` parameter and pools by (proxy,url), so a streamed response keeps the connection open and a later `verify=False` request to the same host reuses it, yielding unverified TLS (CVE-2024-35195).
4. requests/adapters.py:237 — get_connection()/poolmanager keyed only by URL with no verify-aware pool key, the root enabler of the same pool/tls issue.

False positives submitted (1 grouped): Query 2 (sessions.py:171-177 URL/fragment normalization) and Query 3 (sessions.py:235 Cookie header pop; cookies.py:419 `_cookies_lock` pop in `__getstate__`) — probe statements containing no credential handling; the Cookie header is actively stripped, and _cookies_lock is a pickling artifact.
