2026-11-19 21:09:56 - Agent_20261119210411 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed both netrc-related queries (20261119210015, 20261119210136) covering requests 2.30.0. Confirmed CVE-2024-47081 class credential disclosure: get_netrc_auth derives the netrc machine name from urlparse(url).netloc.split(':')[0] instead of the validated hostname (requests/utils.py:230-244), so attacker-crafted URLs with embedded userinfo (e.g. https://internal.corp.example:443@attacker.tld/) cause stored netrc credentials to be sent to an attacker-controlled host. Submitted three true positives for the affected locations: the netrc lookup key derivation / credential return (requests/utils.py:237) and the two call sites that feed untrusted URLs into it (requests/sessions.py:284 rebuild_auth, requests/sessions.py:481 prepare_request). No mitigation or fix is present in this version (verified ri.hostname is never used in get_netrc_auth). Test-file references (tests/test_requests.py) were disregarded as non-exploitable.
